  "_comment": "DCS unit type -> radar specification. THE single home for these numbers. They used to sit alongside the display labels in crc-desktop/app/data/aircraft-types.json, read by nothing but that renderer’s _buildAllRadars(). The radar picture is built server-side now (docs/adr/0042), so they live here and the client file keeps labels only — one home rather than two copies and a parity test. angleFromNose: total scan arc in degrees centred on the nose (360 = a full rotating dish). rangeNm: detection range against a fighter-size target. sweepMs: one full rotation or scan cycle. Every figure is [SOURCE-DEFINED] — DCS publishes none of it, and none of it should be presented as a real aircraft’s performance.",
